"""0031 — repair the meals_v4 batch from its authored source.

Revision: 0031_recipes_quarantine
Author:   nova-backend-architect
Date:     2026-07-17

The `meals_v4` batch (264 recipes, inserted 2026-07-03 21:05:14) is broken
in two independent ways. This restores all 264 from source, fixing both.

BUG 1 — duplicated ingredient, inflated macros (214 recipes). Each carries an
exact-duplicate component row, and its stored macros were computed FROM that
duplicated list. 84% sat outside their slot's kcal band: avg 812 kcal / 77 g
protein, worst a 1452 kcal lunch. A BO user's 2026-07-17 plan served one
("Filete de pescado blanco al horno con pure de papa": 400 g of fish across
two rows, 732 kcal / 96 g protein).

  ROOT CAUSE: the one-off insert script could not parse a non-numeric `qty`
  ("al gusto", for salt/pepper/spices) and, instead of skipping it, emitted a
  duplicate of another ingredient in its place. The correlation is total: of
  the source recipes carrying an "al gusto" ingredient, 201 are broken and
  ZERO are intact. 13 more broke on other unparseable quantities ("1/2").

BUG 2 — zeroed nutrients (all 264). Every recipe in the batch has fiber_g,
sugar_g, sodium_mg and sat_fat_g at 0, because `trg_sync_recipe_aggregates`
(see ORDER below) zeroed them at insert and nothing put them back. Those are
three of the four columns the fatty_liver gate reads (sugar<=8, sat_fat<=5,
fiber>=3), so `fiber >= 3` failed for the whole batch and it was silently
excluded from every fatty_liver plan.

FIX. Not a recompute — a restore from the batch's own authored source, still
in-repo (untracked): data/nova_meals_v4_sample.json plus
nova_meals_v4_nutrient_enrichment.json and nova_meals_v4_micronutrients.json.
All three cover all 264 with values that were authored and reviewed, so
nothing here is invented (CLAUDE.md REGLA PRINCIPAL). The same fish recipe,
in source: 200 g of fish, once, 570 kcal / 46 g protein — in band for lunch.

Restoring puts 262 of the 264 inside their slot band, up from 58 today. The
2 that are not (two 380 kcal dinner soups against a 420 floor) are
quarantined rather than served out of band.

The data is EMBEDDED, not read from data/: docker/api.Dockerfile copies app,
migrations, alembic.ini and scripts — NOT data/ — so a file read would
crash-loop the container on boot. Migration 0030 embeds its snapshot for the
same reason.

ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING. `trg_sync_recipe_aggregates` fires on every
recipe_components write and rewrites recipes.fiber_g/sugar_g/sodium_mg/
sat_fat_g by summing `foods` through `food_id`. These components are free
text with food_id NULL, so that sum is empty and the trigger zeroes all four.
Components must therefore be written BEFORE the nutrition UPDATE, which
targets `recipes` and does not fire the trigger.

GUARD. recipe_components had no uniqueness constraint, which is why the
double-insert landed silently. The new index keys on
(recipe_id, lower(free_text_name), amount_g, coalesce(modifier,'')) with
NULLS NOT DISTINCT (PG 17), rejecting an exact duplicate while still
allowing a legitimate repeat at a different amount or modifier.

KNOWN GAP, deliberate: the 229 "al gusto" ingredients are NOT inserted.
amount_g is nullable and the API types it Optional, but all 5304 existing
rows are non-NULL, and a data repair is the wrong place to hand iOS its
first NULL amount. They are absent from PROD today too, so this is not a
regression. Revisit with the catalog-quality sprint.
"""

